{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03OY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\v C", "ACCENT_0002": "\\v C", "COMMENT_0001": "%9.22.09\n", "GROUPCLOSE_0001": "}", "GROUPCLOSE_0002": "}", "GROUPOPEN_0001": "{", "GROUPOPEN_0002": "{", "MATH_0001": "$\\{\\Spec(B) \\to \\Spec(A)\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$A \\to B$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ea151c96197e63a87604cc6875f3322ff2d8d5b10204fd12365a3c2f8c98da02", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:aa16b291256143f8406deb7dc712d984df0ca350257d79957da4e749a2665f43", "source_text": "\n<COMMENT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe start with a simple lemma (which holds in greater generality than\nstated). It says that the <GROUPOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001><GROUPCLOSE_0001>ech complex of a standard covering is\nequal to the <GROUPOPEN_0002><ACCENT_0002><GROUPCLOSE_0002>ech complex of an fpqc covering of the form\n<MATH_0001> with <MATH_0002> faithfully flat.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:343796c3f8318443f3d05ab91adbe805bc2c9fe37d41a8a15483535a614cbf9d", "unit_id": "tag:03OY:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03OY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\v C", "GROUPCLOSE_0001": "}", "GROUPOPEN_0001": "{", "MATH_0001": "$\\tau \\in \\{fppf, syntomic, smooth, \\etale, Zariski\\}$", "MATH_0002": "$S$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\Sch/S)_\\tau$", "MATH_0005": "$S_\\tau$", "MATH_0006": "$\\tau = \\etale$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{U} = \\{U_i \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\tau$", "MATH_0009": "$V = \\coprod_{i \\in I} U_i$", "MATH_0010": "$V$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{V} = \\{V \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0012": "$\\tau$", "MATH_0013": "$\\tau = Zariski$", "MATH_0014": "$\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^\\bullet (\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0015": "$\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^\\bullet (\\mathcal{V}, \\mathcal{F})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-cech-complex}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:6c11b88931348efe8137d655c9526e51799f59ec89617591b23555ee463075ce", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:502185e2cf0f5893dbad32dd7aa6241914ae180e929bac4cae36a39a9587a3ab", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a scheme.\nLet <MATH_0003> be an abelian sheaf on <MATH_0004>, or on\n<MATH_0005> in case <MATH_0006>, and let\n<MATH_0007>\nbe a standard <MATH_0008>-covering of this site.\nLet <MATH_0009>. Then\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0010> is an affine scheme,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0011> is an fpqc covering\nand also a <MATH_0012>-covering unless <MATH_0013>,\n<STRUCT_0004> the <GROUPOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001><GROUPCLOSE_0001>ech complexes\n<MATH_0014> and\n<MATH_0015> agree.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8f455b47aac538e52066744028322520762c9f34b25215406ed97190