{"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03OY", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\v C", "ACCENT_0002": "\\v C", "GROUPCLOSE_0001": "}", "GROUPCLOSE_0002": "}", "GROUPOPEN_0001": "{", "GROUPOPEN_0002": "{", "MATH_0001": "$\\tau$", "MATH_0002": "$U_i$", "MATH_0003": "$I$", "MATH_0004": "$V$", "MATH_0005": "$V \\to U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{V}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{V}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\tau$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{U}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{V}$", "MATH_0011": "$\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^\\bullet (\\mathcal{V}, \\mathcal{F}) \\to\n\\check{\\mathcal{C}}^\\bullet (\\mathcal{U}, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0012": "$T = \\coprod_{j \\in J} T_j$", "MATH_0013": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0014": "$\\{T_j \\to T\\}_{j \\in J}$", "MATH_0015": "\\begin{equation}\n\\label{equation-sheaf-coprod}\n\\mathcal{F}(T) =\n\\mathcal{F}(\\coprod\\nolimits_{j \\in J} T_j) =\n\\prod\\nolimits_{j \\in J} \\mathcal{F}(T_j)\n\\end{equation}", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0017": "$$\nV \\times_U \\ldots \\times_U V\n=\n\\coprod\\nolimits_{i_0, \\ldots i_p} U_{i_0} \\times_U \\ldots \\times_U U_{i_p}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{topologies-definition-standard-Zariski}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topologies-definition-standard-etale}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{topologies-definition-standard-smooth}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{topologies-definition-standard-syntomic}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{topologies-definition-standard-fppf}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{example-fpqc-coverings}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{topologies-definition-etale-covering}", "REF_0008": "\\ref{topologies-definition-smooth-covering}", "REF_0009": "\\ref{topologies-definition-syntomic-covering}", "REF_0010": "\\ref{topologies-definition-fppf-covering}", "REF_0011": "\\ref{sites-cohomology-equation-map-cech-complexes}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0002": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e05b69b9a911880ec956a936696ba80f17efe54cf5c163db7b7ee4a2cd30d9b9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2f0b6c3fc0826a5fa40a00e80a7206da12f7f8a0234488a4c52ecb964f824d6f", "source_text": "The definition of a standard <MATH_0001>-covering is given in\nTopologies, Definition\n<REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>,\n<REF_0003>,\n<REF_0004>, and\n<REF_0005>.\nBy definition each of the schemes\n<MATH_0002> is affine and <MATH_0003> is a finite set. Hence <MATH_0004> is an affine scheme.\nIt is clear that <MATH_0005> is flat and surjective, hence\n<MATH_0006> is an fpqc covering, see\nExample <REF_0006>.\nExcepting the Zariski case, the covering <MATH_0007>\nis also a <MATH_0008>-covering, see\nTopologies, Definition\n<REF_0007>,\n<REF_0008>,\n<REF_0009>, and\n<REF_0010>.\n\n<STRUCT_0001><STRUCT_0002>\nNote that <MATH_0009> is a refinement of <MATH_0010>\nand hence there is a map of <GROUPOPEN_0001><ACCENT_0001><GROUPCLOSE_0001>ech complexes\n<MATH_0011>, see\nCohomology on Sites,\nEquation (<REF_0011>).\nNext, we observe that if <MATH_0012> is a\ndisjoint union of schemes in the site on which <MATH_0013> is defined\nthen the family of morphisms with fixed target\n<MATH_0014> is a Zariski covering, and so\n<MATH_0015>\nby the sheaf condition of <MATH_0016>.\nThis implies the map of <GROUPOPEN_0002><ACCENT_0002><GROUPCLOSE_0002>ech complexes above is an isomorphism\nin each degree because\n<MATH_0017>\nas schemes.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:78a6f8efab8cf0f5bbf31d269f0d480f2f9c5badc30430a6ae3d4010bf78ede0", "unit_id": "tag:03OZ:proof"}
